From d5877ad727a6ac7f7050ae5086e4f9751e25b89d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 05:05:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the board Worker fail closed instead of trusting Access
 alone

The Worker carried a comment saying it deliberately does not re-check
identity, because Access would already have allowed the request and a second
check would be security theatre. That reasoning assumed Access was configured.
On 2026-09-06 it was not: the Worker was live on its workers.dev URL with no
policy in front of it, and the only reason nothing leaked is that the R2
bucket was still empty. One unticked dashboard box was the entire control over
lead names, phone numbers and coverage notes.

/api/* now verifies the Access JWT itself -- RS256 signature against the
team's JWKS, aud, iss, exp, nbf -- and refuses whenever it cannot:

  * ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN or ACCESS_AUD unset -> 503, no bucket read at all.
    Unconfigured means closed. This is what makes the bad window impossible
    rather than merely unlikely.
  * missing/invalid/expired token -> 403, with no reason given, since a
    verification oracle only helps whoever is probing.

The static shell stays unauthenticated: it holds no customer data, and letting
it load means a misconfiguration surfaces as a visible error rather than a
blank page nobody looks into.

Defence in depth, not a replacement for Access.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
